{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017LksnnS3w2DQ9JQcySua6H","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Issue 2: Splitting a damage charge two ways loses a cent\n2\t\n3\t## Outcome\n4\t\n5\tEvery penny of a damage charge is billed to someone. The shares from `splitCharge` add up to the\n6\tcharge. Charge D-301 (3333 cents) split two ways gives 1667 and 1666 cents, not 1666 and 1666.\n7\t\n8\t## Requirements\n9\t\n10\t- When a charge does not divide evenly by the number of borrowers, the system shall give each borrower the rounded-down share and hand out the leftover cents one each, starting with the first borrower.\n11\t- The system shall return shares that add up to exactly the charge, for every charge and number of borrowers.\n12\t- The system shall return shares that differ from each other by at most one cent.\n13\t- When a charge divides evenly, the system shall give every borrower the same share.\n14\t\n15\t## Must not change\n16\t\n17\t- Amounts stay integer cents. No floats.\n18\t- `splitCharge(totalCents, ways)` keeps its name, arguments and return type (`number[]` of length `ways`).\n19\t- A negative or non-integer charge, or fewer than one borrower, is still refused with an error.\n20\t- Nothing under `src/auth/` changes.\n21\t- The existing tests in `tests/fees/split.test.ts` stay as they are.\n22\t\n23\t## Out of scope\n24\t\n25\t- Late fees (`src/fees/late.ts`).\n26\t- Weighted or unequal splits.\n27\t- Changes to how `bun run desk split` prints amounts.\n28\t\n29\t## Done when\n30\t\n31\t- The new tests in `tests/fees/split.test.ts` pass, and so do the existing ones.\n32\t- `bun run gate` exits 0.\n33\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bcd83ddb-e2cd-4f53-9c41-6ff13ba26c5c","uuid":"74c754a0-015f-426b-812b-a532a511be64","timestamp":"2026-11-14T16:29:11.126Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/user/software-factory-claude-code/parts/06-price-and-ship/03-ship-the-factory/solution/rerun/runs/2/repo/specs/2/SPEC.md","content":"# Issue 2: Splitting a damage charge two ways loses a cent\n\n## Outcome\n\nEvery penny of a damage charge is billed to someone. The shares from `splitCharge` add up to the\ncharge. Charge D-301 (3333 cents) split two ways gives 1667 and 1666 cents, not 1666 and 1666.\n\n## Requirements\n\n- When a charge does not divide evenly by the number of borrowers, the system shall give each borrower the rounded-down share and hand out the leftover cents one each, starting with the first borrower.\n- The system shall return shares that add up to exactly the charge, for every charge and number of borrowers.\n- The system shall return shares that differ from each other by at most one cent.\n- When a charge divides evenly, the system shall give every borrower the same share.\n\n## Must not change\n\n- Amounts stay integer cents. No floats.\n- `splitCharge(totalCents, ways)` keeps its name, arguments and return type (`number[]` of length `ways`).\n- A negative or non-integer charge, or fewer than one borrower, is still refused with an error.\n- Nothing under `src/auth/` changes.\n- The existing tests in `tests/fees/split.test.ts` stay as they are.\n\n## Out of scope\n\n- Late fees (`src/fees/late.ts`).\n- Weighted or unequal splits.\n- Changes to how `bun run desk split` prints amounts.\n\n## Done when\n\n- The new tests in `tests/fees/split.test.ts` pass, and so do the existing ones.\n- `bun run gate` exits 0.\n","numLines":33,"startLine":1,"totalLines":33}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_017LksnnS3w2DQ9JQcySua6H","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
